# tools/f/font5x7_tilde_comp_witness.rish -- the tilde vowels GROWN by composition prove themselves on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) - the fourth accent mark grown rather than drawn, after the grave (glyph_accent),
# the acute (font5x7_acute), and the circumflex (font5x7_circumflex_comp). image/font5x7_tilde_comp.rye grows the a/o
# tilde set (U+00E3, U+00F5) by overlaying a single wave onto the lowercase base through a two-row table. The crux this
# witness proves: each composed tilde vowel equals the hand-drawn image/font5x7_tilde.rye's own coverage BYTE-FOR-BYTE,
# and the composed atlas round-trips through the gfa1 encoder/decoder byte-for-byte -- so the corpus grown by
# composition IS the corpus drawn by hand. Only the two nasal vowels are composed; the n tilde rides a consonant base
# and lives hand-drawn in font5x7_latin1. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/f/font5x7_tilde_comp_witness.rish

say "font5x7-tilde-comp: Language EN -- Season G open-media primitive; the tilde vowels grown by composition from one wave and a two-row table over the lowercase base, the O(letters + accents) economy proven on a fourth mark (grave, acute, circumflex, now tilde)."
say "font5x7-tilde-comp: Style Radiant -- the hand-drawn tilde corpus is the specification; the composed vowels equal its coverage byte-for-byte and round-trip through gfa1 byte-identical, so a corpus grown by composition is the corpus drawn by hand, our own open font, no external font to license."
say "font5x7-tilde-comp: Lens TAME -- u32 in-memory counts; the table bounded; accented codepoints strictly ascending (the order the encoder trusts); invariants positive (parity per row, the base present, the wave spanning both halves and cresting right); refusals named; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/font5x7_tilde_comp"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/font5x7_tilde_comp.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "font5x7-tilde-comp: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "font5x7-tilde-comp: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "font5x7-tilde-comp: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-font5x7-tilde-comp" else "font5x7-tilde-comp: selftest did not print the GREEN corpus line"
